  "notes": "Illustrative per-op microbenchmarks for an edge-class ARM board (median of repeated runs under int8 kernels). Representative values used for the hackathon demo; replace the table with on-device measurements without changing any other code. Fairness gap: convolutions are trained with group-aware batching and incur a small disparity gap per unit of capacity, while pooling/identity layers carry the gap of the activations they pass through (higher gap per capacity unit) — this is what makes convs, pools and skips trade off against each other on the fairness objective instead of one op dominating."
